<h2 id="faq-heading">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="usa-accordion usa-accordion--bordered usa-accordion--multiselectable" data-allow-multiple="">
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-1">Why do cookie lines need special conveyors?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-1" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Cookies and crackers break from impact, compression, and vibration. Standard conveyors create all three. Cookie lines use low back-pressure <a href="/conveyor-types/accumulation-conveyors/">accumulation</a>, close-gap transfers, and servo-timed infeed to keep breakage low.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-2">What is a counter stacker?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-2" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>A counter stacker counts individual cookies on a high-speed belt, forms them into stacks of a specified count, and delivers the stack to a wrapper. Rated speed depends on product size and machine model. See also: <a href="/conveyor-functions/stacking-machines/">stacking machines</a>.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-3">How do you prevent cookie breakage?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-3" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Eliminate hard transfer points with tapered nose rollers or zero-gap transfers. Use low back-pressure accumulation (Slip-Torque rollers stop under stopped product). Maintain gentle speed differentials. Use soft belt surfaces. Set a breakage target and measure breakage at each transfer.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-4">What is slug-wrap packaging?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-4" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Slug-wrap wraps a horizontal stack of cookies in film using a HFFS (horizontal form-fill-seal) machine. The slug conveyor delivers counted stacks at precise spacing and speed. Standard for sandwich cookies, thin crackers, and premium brands.</p>

</div>
